{"design": "neg_twos6b", "family": "negate", "reward": 0.0, "compile_ok": false, "rtl": "The `neg_twos6b` module computes the two's complement negation of a 6-bit input. The module is implemented using a simple 6-bit full adder with a subtractive input set to 1. The full adder is implemented using an XOR gate, AND gates, and a full 6-bit ripple carry adder (RC adder). \n\nThe XOR gate takes the input and the subtractive input, and computes the two's complement of the input. The other input of the XOR gate is the result of the 6-bit ripple carry adder, which adds 1 to the two's complement of the input. \n\nThe output of the module is registered on the positive edge of the `clk` signal. The `rst_n` input is used to clear the output on the first clock cycle after reset.\n\n```\nmodule neg_twos6b (\n    input  wire clk, rst_n,\n    input  wire [5:0] in,\n    output reg  [5:0] out\n);\n\n    // Register inputs\n    reg [5:0] in_reg;\n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        if (!rst_n) begin\n            in_reg <= 6'd0;\n        end else begin\n            in_reg <= in;\n        end\n    end\n\n    // Compute two's complement negation\n    wire [5:0] neg_in;\n    assign neg_in = ~in_reg + 1;\n\n    // Compute ripple carry adder\n    wire [5:0] rc_adder_out;\n    wire [5:0] rc_adder_carry;\n    assign rc_adder_carry = {1'b1, 5'b00000};\n    ripple_carry_adder_6bit rc_adder (\n        .a(neg_in),\n        .b(rc_adder_carry),\n        .sum(rc_adder_out),\n        .cout()\n    );\n\n    // Compute full adder\n    wire [5:0] full_adder_out;\n    assign"}
